  "title": "Kommet, ihr Hirten",
  "composer": "Traditional",
  "about": "Kommet, ihr Hirten means Come, you shepherds in German. The song comes from Bohemia, where its Czech title is Nesem vám noviny. The tune was first printed in 1847, in a Catholic hymnal in Olomouc. The Leipzig conductor Carl Riedel wrote the German words freely after the original, and first printed them in 1870.",
  "funFact": "The scholar Konrad Ameln dated the tune to around 1700 from its style alone.",
